.TH stmakui "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
stmakui \- WebKit container for the LinuxCNC web user interfaces

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stmakui
.BI \-\-url " URL"
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fIW\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR \fIH\fR]
.br
.B stmakui
.BI \-\-path " PATH"
[\fB\-\-instance\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-xid\fR \fIXID\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fIW\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR \fIH\fR]
.br
.I front-end-name
(via symlink)

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stmakui
opens a single GTK/WebKit window and loads a LinuxCNC web application
served by
.BR stmakd (1).
It is the native-window front end for the web-based HAL and machine
utilities.
.PP
When invoked as
.B stmakui
directly, the page to load must be given with
.B \-\-url
or
.BR \-\-path .
When invoked through a symlink, the basename of the link selects a
built-in application profile that supplies the URL path, window title
and window size.  The following profile names are built in:
.TP
.B halscope
HAL Oscilloscope
.TP
.B halshow
HAL Show
.TP
.B emccalib
EMC Calibration
.TP
.B tooledit
Tool Editor
.TP
.B latency
RT Latency test application
.TP
.B linuxcnctop-ui
LinuxCNC Status window (the viewer that bare
.B linuxcnctop
execs into)
.TP
.B classicladder
Classic Ladder editor (addresses the
.B classicladder
instance instead of the
.B milltask
default)
.PP
The server base URL is taken from the
.B STMAK_REST_URL
environment variable (default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:5080 ).
Positional arguments are ignored, so callers that pass a file path
(e.g. AXIS embedding hooks) work unchanged.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url " \fIURL\fR"
Load
.I URL
instead of a built-in profile.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " \fIPATH\fR"
Load the page
.I PATH
of the server, e.g.
.BR app/halshow/ .
The base URL and the
.B ?instance=
parameter are added as for a built-in profile.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-url .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instance " \fINAME\fR"
Instance name for the
.B ?instance=
parameter; overrides
.B STMAK_TASK_INSTANCE
and the profile default.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-xid " \fIXID\fR"
Embed the view into the X window
.I XID
(XEmbed) instead of opening a window of its own; see
.BR "EMBEDDED MODE" .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " \fITITLE\fR"
Window title.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-width " \fIW\fR"
Window width in pixels.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-height " \fIH\fR"
Window height in pixels.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and the list of known application profiles.

.SH "EMBEDDED MODE"
With
.BR \-\-xid ,
.B stmakui
runs inside another program's window.
AXIS uses this for web application tabs
.RB ( "EMBED_TAB_COMMAND = webapp" " \fIPATH\fR)"
and for its web application side panel
.RB ( WEBAPP_PANEL ),
see
.BR axis (1).
Embedding needs an X11 display (XWayland included).
.PP
Tk, which AXIS is built on, does not hand the keyboard to an embedded
window, so
.B stmakui
takes it itself when the page is clicked; the embedding program takes it
back when one of its own widgets is clicked.
Keys the page does not use itself are passed on to the window named by
.BR AXIS_FORWARD_EVENTS_TO ,
so AXIS shortcuts such as Escape keep working while the page has the
keyboard. Every passed-on key press is followed by its release, also when
the page loses the keyboard while the key is held.
.PP
If the server cannot be reached, the page shows a waiting note and is
loaded again with a growing delay (1 to 10 seconds) until the server
answers. A crashed web process is restarted the same way.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STMAK_REST_URL
Base URL of the stmakd REST interface (default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:5080 ).
.TP
.B STMAK_TASK_INSTANCE
Instance name appended as
.B ?instance=
to profile URLs; overrides the profile default (usually
.BR milltask ).
.TP
.B AXIS_FORWARD_EVENTS_TO
In embedded mode, the X window ID that keys not used by the page are
sent to. AXIS sets it to its main window.

